buffers of its views not released. confirmed is the count a"] [30 1 "// collection last found held (-1, or any other value than n, once the count moved since): a refusal at that count"] [31 1 "// asks the collector nothing more, so a view held over many refused resizes costs one collection, not one each."] [34 1 "// BufferExporter is an exporter that counts its exports (builtinValue of a subclass's instance answers too)."] [37 1 "// Count is the exports held (a view not released, or not yet found dead)."] [40 1 "// Refuse is the exporter's check before it changes its buffer's size: nil while nothing holds an export (after the"] [41 1 "// collector found the views dropped unreleased dead), else BufferError msg (arraymodule.c's \"cannot resize an array"] [42 1 "// that is exporting buffers\", bytearray's \"Existing exports of data: object cannot be re-sized\")."] [53 1 "// Acquire and Release are a native's own export over a call (PyObject_GetBuffer ... PyBuffer_Release), for an"] [54 1 "// exporter whose buffer must not move while the call holds it."] [69 1 "// exportsOf is o's count, nil when o (or the built-in value of a subclass's instance) counts none."] [80 1 "// managedBuffer is _PyManagedBufferObject: one export of an exporter, shared by the views made from the first."] [82 23 "// the exporter's count (nil: the exporter counts none)"] [83 23 "// the views registered and not released (mbuf->exports)"] [84 2 "// a class's __buffer__ (PEP 688, slot_bf_getbuffer): the exporter and the view its __buffer__ returned, the"] [85 2 "// export held as typeobject.c's _PyBufferWrapper holds it (memory_getbuf of the view)"] [88 2 "// slot_bf_releasebuffer over a built-in exporter (queue 475): the object whose class's Python __release_buffer__"] [89 2 "// is called with a restricted view of master when the export goes, before the built-in's release (exp)"] [92 2 "// release is a Py_buffer's PyBuffer_Release (queue 473: a C exporter's view, kept in place; a memoryview's"] [93 2 "// __buffer__ export of itself), called once the last view goes"] [97 1 "// newManagedBuffer is the export memoryview(o) takes: o's count raised when it counts."] [101 3 "// PYI_NO_FINALIZERS: no view is ever found dead, so none counts (pyi's behaviour before 249)"] [108 1 "// register makes v a view of mb (mbuf_add_view): it holds the export until released or dead."] [119 1 "// drop is mbuf_release: the export given back once the last view went (PyBuffer_Release of the master: the exporter's"] [120 1 "// bf_releasebuffer)."] [122 40 "// slot_bf_releasebuffer: the Python method first, then the base's release"] [144 1 "// bufferwrapperReleasebuf is typeobject.c's bufferwrapper_releasebuf, then bufferwrapper_dealloc (queue 475): the"] [145 1 "// view __buffer__ returned gives its export back (memory_releasebuf); the class's Python __release_buffer__ is called"] [146 1 "// with that view when the view is not of the object itself (a view of the object, super().__buffer__'s, is released"] [147 1 "// by its own export's release, slot_bf_releasebuffer's, below). The wrapper then drops its reference to the view;"] [148 1 "// pyi has no reference counts, so a view of the object itself, which only the wrapper held in CPython's usual case"] [149 1 "// (__buffer__ returning super().__buffer__(flags)), is released here as its dealloc would, when nothing else exports"] [150 1 "// from it."] [154 2 "// a built-in's __buffer__ called on a subclass's instance gets the built-in value (a method descriptor's self)"] [164 2 "// its dealloc's mbuf_release: PyBuffer_Release of the object's own export, slot_bf_releasebuffer when the class's"] [165 2 "// __release_buffer__ is Python's (the export made of the built-in value has no slot of its own), then the base's"] [175 1 "// memoryviewFinalize is memory_dealloc's release of a view never released: its export given back."] [187 1 "// exportsVerify is the collection at a refused resize: Go's collection and the finalizers' drain (finRound) while it"] [188 1 "// gives exports back, within the collections' budget; whether e still exports (false also past the budget, or while"] [189 1 "// finalizers are draining: the resize then allowed). A count found held is confirmed until it moves."] [216 1 "// exportsRound is finRound's collection with a shorter wait: Go's collection, then a wait until a dead object is"] [217 1 "// queued or Go's finalizers have been still for 3 ms (polled every 100 us), then the drain. A view dropped unreleased"] [218 1 "// is queued as soon as Go's finalizer goroutine runs, so the common case (a temporary view) costs the collection"] [219 1 "// alone; a view still held costs the 3 ms once (BufferExports.confirmed)."] [243 2 "// exportsSpent is the time the refused resizes' collections took: held to a tenth of the elapsed wall time and"] [244 2 "// 200 ms, the moment at del's rule (finSpent, queue 222) with a budget of its own"] [246 2 "// PYI_EXPORTS_DEBUG=1: each verification's rounds on stderr"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[71 32] [74 46] [122 24] [130 20] [132 16] [155 20] [170 23] [182 23] [199 16] [199 38] [224 28] [224 57] [232 28]]} (go/file "buffer_export.go" :imports [


